\section{Source-Shaped Lyapunov Funnel Capture of the Live MEKF}
\label{sec:finite-live-capture}

The Live handoff certificate uses the exact compact set produced by startup only
at the initial inclusion step.  Thereafter it propagates verified Lyapunov
funnel levels over source-reachable words rather than repeatedly enclosing the
full 18--21 dimensional reachable set.  This avoids set-wrapping growth while
retaining the complete nonlinear source map, including finite attitude
corrections, the full $S=0$ cross-gain, covariance recursion, and mode changes.

\subsection{Exact lifted source image and proof-safe domains}

Let $\pi$ contain the complete source proof state: covariance,
accelerometer-bias enable state, magnetic-gauge state, staged or Live OU/$R_S$
parameters, pseudo-update phase, accepted-update pattern, and source guards.
For any admissible lift of $m\ge1$ samples write the implemented error map as
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \vct e_{k+m}=\mathcal F_{k,m}
 (\vct e_k,\vct d_{k:k+m-1};\pi_{k:k+m}).}
 \label{eq:capture-exact-lift}
\end{equation}
It contains exact prediction, accepted accelerometer and magnetometer
corrections, the full $S=0$ Kalman correction and attitude cross-covariance,
quaternion injection/reset, covariance propagation, source enable-state
transitions, and the predictable parameter schedule.

For hybrid and prefix-safety statements it is convenient to name the exact
image operator
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathfrak T_{k,m}(X;\bar d):=
 \left\{
 \mathcal F_{k,m}(e,d;\pi):
 e\in X,\ \|d\|_\infty\le\bar d,\
 \pi\in\Pi^{\rm src}_{k,m}
 \right\}.}
 \label{eq:capture-set-envelope}
\end{equation}
The operator is a definition of the exact source image; the capture verifier
does not recursively replace that image by a radius box or by a generic outer
reachable set.

Let $\mathcal D_i$ be the proof-safe domain of source node $i$, including its
geodesic attitude chart, covariance domain, measurement gates, and physical
state bounds.  The fixed-dimensional normal-Live nodes and source-complete word
families are those of Sec.~\ref{sec:stability-widening-source-path}.  A
mode-changing source transition has its own exact jump map and destination node
metric.

\subsection{Node funnels and word contraction}

Use the group/path metric
\begin{equation}
 W_i(e)=a_{R,i}V_R(\mat R_e)+\vct\xi^\top\mat P_i\vct\xi
 \label{eq:capture-funnel-metric}
\end{equation}
from Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-group-metric}.  For a level $c_i\ge0$ define the
source-node funnel section
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal F_i(c_i):=\{e\in\mathcal D_i:W_i(e)\le c_i\}.}
 \label{eq:capture-funnel-section}
\end{equation}
For every certified source word $w:i\to j$ require a robust endpoint inequality
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_j(\mathcal F_w(e,d))
 \le\lambda_w W_i(e)+\gamma_w(\bar d),
 \qquad 0\le\lambda_w<1,}
 \label{eq:capture-funnel-word}
\end{equation}
for all $e$ in the admitted source-node funnel and all
$\|d\|_\infty\le\bar d$.  Every strict sample prefix of the same word must
remain in its corresponding proof-safe source domain:
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathfrak T^{\rm pre}_{w,s}(\mathcal F_i(c_i);\bar d)
 \subseteq\mathcal D_{i_s},
 \qquad 1\le s<\ell(w).}
 \label{eq:capture-prefix-domain}
\end{equation}
Positive one-sample Lyapunov increments are allowed inside a word.

Dimension-changing or hard-reset transitions use the same form with the exact
jump/lift map $J:i\to j$ and the destination metric:
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_j(J(e,d))\le\lambda_JW_i(e)+\gamma_J(\bar d),}
 \label{eq:capture-funnel-jump}
\end{equation}
where the source transition need not be square and no homogeneous matrix product
is formed across the dimension change.

\subsection{Source-shaped handoff funnel}

Let
\begin{equation}
 X_0:=\mathcal H_{k_H}
 \label{eq:capture-handoff-set}
\end{equation}
be the exact compact handoff family supplied by the startup analysis.  If the
handoff can enter several source nodes, define for each such node
\begin{equation}
 c_{0,i}:=
 \sup_{e\in\mathcal H_{k_H}\cap\mathcal D_i}W_i(e),
 \label{eq:capture-initial-level}
\end{equation}
with $c_{0,i}=-\infty$ for an unreachable node.  The required initial
inclusion is therefore
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal H_{k_H}\subseteq\bigcup_i\mathcal F_i(c_{0,i})
 \subseteq\bigcup_i\mathcal D_i.}
 \label{eq:capture-handoff-inclusion}
\end{equation}
This retains the actual source-shaped handoff set without embedding it in a
single Euclidean outer ball.

Propagate only verified scalar funnel levels.  For every destination node $j$
define
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 c_{n+1,j}:=
 \max_{w:i\to j\ \mathrm{reachable}}
 \left\{\lambda_w c_{n,i}+\gamma_w(\bar d)\right\},}
 \label{eq:capture-funnel-recursion}
\end{equation}
where the maximum includes certified dimension-changing transition words and is
taken only over source-reachable incoming words.  An unreachable destination
retains level $-\infty$.  Equation~\eqref{eq:capture-funnel-word} implies that
every exact source image represented by level $c_{n,i}$ lies in the destination
funnel represented by $c_{n+1,j}$.

Choose terminal inner levels $b_i>0$ and define
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal B_i:=\mathcal F_i(b_i),
 \qquad
 \mathcal B:=\bigcup_i\mathcal B_i.
 \label{eq:capture-inner-funnel}
\end{equation}
They are robustly invariant when every reachable certified word or jump obeys
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \lambda_w b_i+\gamma_w(\bar d)\le b_j.}
 \label{eq:capture-inner-invariance}
\end{equation}
Let
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 N_H:=\min\{n:c_{n,i}\le b_i\ \text{for every reachable node }i\}.}
 \label{eq:capture-count}
\end{equation}
If all certified words have length at most $\ell_+$ and the sample period is at
most $h_+$, then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{T_H\le h_+\ell_+N_H.}
 \label{eq:capture-time}
\end{equation}

\begin{theorem}[Source-shaped Lyapunov-funnel Live capture and practical ISS]
\label{thm:finite-live-capture}
Assume the source-complete path certificate of
Theorem~\ref{thm:widen-path-direct-iss}, the handoff inclusion
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-handoff-inclusion}, the robust word/jump inequalities
Eqs.~\eqref{eq:capture-funnel-word} and \eqref{eq:capture-funnel-jump}, and the
prefix-safety condition Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-prefix-domain}.  If the funnel
recursion has finite $N_H$ and the terminal levels satisfy
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-inner-invariance}, then every deterministic Live
trajectory starting in $\mathcal H_{k_H}$ remains proof safe, enters
$\mathcal B$ after at most $N_H$ certified words/transitions, and remains in the
inner funnel thereafter.

Let
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_B:=\max_w\lambda_w<1,
 \qquad
 \gamma_B(\bar d):=\max_w\gamma_w(\bar d).
 \label{eq:capture-inner-contraction}
\end{equation}
At post-capture word index $r$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 W_r\le\lambda_B^rW_0
 +\frac{1-\lambda_B^r}{1-\lambda_B}\gamma_B(\bar d).}
 \label{eq:capture-practical-iss}
\end{equation}
For $\bar d=0$, the certified word-boundary error converges exponentially to the
adopted gauge, with sample-prefix boundedness supplied by the certified word
prefixes.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
The initial inclusion places every source handoff in a node funnel.  Apply the
appropriate robust word or jump inequality to each possible source transition;
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-funnel-recursion} is the worst jointly reachable endpoint
level and therefore contains every exact endpoint image.  Prefix safety keeps
all intermediate samples inside the proof domains.  Induction gives
$c_{n,i}$ at every reachable node.  Finite $N_H$ gives entry into the terminal
inner funnels, Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-inner-invariance} gives forward invariance,
and iteration with the uniform maxima gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-practical-iss}.
\end{proof}

\subsection{Diagnostic summaries and operational certificate contract}
\label{sec:capture-certificate-contract}

For reporting only, a verifier may summarize any compact set $X$ by selected
physical or dimensionless coordinate radii.  Denote such a diagnostic map by
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal R_k(X):=
 \left(\sup_{e\in X}r_{1,k}(e),\ldots,
       \sup_{e\in X}r_{q,k}(e)\right)^\top.
 \label{eq:capture-radius-enclosure}
\end{equation}
These numbers are not propagated and are not certificate state variables.

The verifier starts at the exact covariance and source mode produced by
\texttt{goLive()}, including the enabled linear block, staged OU parameters,
full $S=0$ gain, pseudo-update phase, and accelerometer-bias hold.  It reports at
least
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \{\mathcal H,\mathcal D_i,W_i,\mathscr W_{\rm src},
 c_{0,i},c_{n,i},b_i,N_H,T_H,B_{\rm pre},
 \lambda_w,\gamma_w\}.}
 \label{eq:capture-certificate-outputs}
\end{equation}
The deterministic pass conditions are
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal H_{k_H}\subseteq\bigcup_i\mathcal D_i,
 \qquad
 N_H<\infty,
 \qquad
 c_{N_H,i}\le b_i\ \text{for every reachable }i,}
 \label{eq:capture-certificate-pass}
\end{equation}
together with rigorous word/jump inequalities, prefix safety, and inner-funnel
invariance.  Sampling trajectories is not sufficient to establish these
suprema; the continuous source families must be enclosed by validated
arithmetic, robust optimization, or another rigorous enclosure method.

\subsection{Stochastic Live qualification}
\label{sec:capture-stochastic}

Gaussian process and measurement noise are not represented by a deterministic
infinite-horizon supremum.  Let $\mathscr F_n$ be the filtration at certified
word boundaries and let $W_n$ be the same nonnegative funnel Lyapunov measure.

\begin{theorem}[Mean-square practical stability under stochastic Live noise]
\label{thm:capture-stochastic-live}
Assume the exact stochastic lifted map remains in the certified stochastic
funnel domain and satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathbb E[W_{n+1}\mid\mathscr F_n]
 \le\lambda_sW_n+\sigma_s^2,
 \qquad 0<\lambda_s<1.}
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-drift}
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathbb EW_n
 \le\lambda_s^n\mathbb EW_0
 +\frac{1-\lambda_s^n}{1-\lambda_s}\sigma_s^2.}
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-ms}
\end{equation}
Moreover, for any $a>0$ and finite horizon $N$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \Pr\!\left(\max_{0\le n\le N}W_n\ge a\right)
 \le\frac1a\sum_{n=0}^{N}\left(
 \lambda_s^n\mathbb EW_0+
 \frac{\sigma_s^2}{1-\lambda_s}\right).}
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-finite-hp}
\end{equation}
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Taking expectations in Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-drift} and iterating
gives Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-ms}.  Markov's inequality followed by a
union bound over the finite horizon gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-finite-hp}.
\end{proof}

Equation~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-drift} is a stochastic certificate
condition for the exact implemented word map; it is not inferred from the
deterministic bounded-input theorem.
